evitaDB stemmers
----------------

src/lib/knowledge/stemming/czech.ts, slovak.ts, polish.ts and romanian.ts
are TypeScript ports of the variant stemmers in evitaDB
(https://github.com/FgForrest/evitaDB, io.evitadb.index.fulltext.analysis:
CzechVariantStemmer, SlovakVariantStemmer, PolishVariantStemmer,
RomanianVariantStemmer; pull request #1453), copyright (c) 2026 FG Forrest,
a.s. FG Forrest, a.s., the copyright holder, contributes these ports to
Riffado under Riffado's license.

Apache Lucene
-------------

The Czech stemmer's ending tables are those of Lucene's CzechStemmer
(org.apache.lucene.analysis.cz), an implementation of the light stemmer of
Ljiljana Dolamic and Jacques Savoy, "Indexing and stemming approaches for
the Czech language" (Information Processing & Management 45(6), 2009).
The Polish and Romanian stemmers read the rules of the Snowball stemmers as
Lucene ships them. Apache Lucene, copyright The Apache Software Foundation,
is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Snowball
--------

The Polish and Romanian rules come from the Snowball project
(https://snowballstem.org), copyright (c) Dr Martin Porter and Richard
Boulton and others, licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.

The stemmers in src/lib/knowledge/stemming/snowball are the JavaScript the
Snowball 3.1.1 release generates (scripts/snowball-stemmers.sh rebuilds and
checks them), under the same license; its text is in
src/lib/knowledge/stemming/snowball/COPYING.

